A||||3||Gokart||Identifying a manual tranny||||5||
Z||000000||Gokart||09-06-2000||08:03 PM||||I pulled the 2.8 with tranny attached today out of my parts car. The Fiero is a 86 2M4 originally but the previous(deceased)owner put in a V6 from another Fiero. Are there any identifiable marks or something to look for on the tranny to tell me if it was a 4spd/5spd Getrag/Isuzu? Thanks!!!<P>Marc 87GT <A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com/gokart/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com/gokart/</A> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||rockcrawl||09-06-2000||08:45 PM||||It's either the Chilton's or Haynes book that has pictures of the muncie and the Isuzu, and they are labeled incorrectly, so be carefull. I can tell them apart by looking at them, but its hard to describe them without showing you a picture. Somebody here must have some pictures!<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'86 GT 3800 (for sale)<BR>'87 GT (noisey 2.8)<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)||||reg||4
Z||000002||pherder||09-06-2000||08:57 PM||||Gokart,<P>How did the shift cables route?<P>If both came over the top of the transaxle, it is an Isuzu 5 speed.<P>If they came up to the shifter mechanism, one from the bottom and the other from the top, then it is a Getrag/Muncie 5 speed.<P>I haven't a clue what a 4 speed has ... haven't had one since 1983!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  (yes, a brand new 1984 that I leased in 1983!)<P>Paul||||reg||1
Z||000003||Gokart||09-06-2000||10:12 PM||||Bingo <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> 5spd Isuzu! Thanks pherder!||||reg||14
